WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:10.735
This video shows how an admin creates an exam on a phone. A short wizard asks for the details, the classes and a date sheet, and then shows a preview.

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:21.794
Tap the menu button at the top left, open Academics, and then choose Exams. The exams that already exist are listed as cards.

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:31.042
Tap Create Exam at the top of the page. The Create Exam Group wizard opens, with four steps shown along the top.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:45.564
Step one is the details. The academic year is already chosen. Pick the term and the exam type, and then set the start and end dates. The exam name fills in by itself from your choices.

00:00:51.344 --> 00:00:57.008
Tap Next. Step two asks which classes will sit this exam.

00:00:59.825 --> 00:01:09.545
Tick the class, here Class 1 - A, which shows its three subjects. Tap Next to reach the date sheet, where the wizard gives each subject a day.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:25.426
Tap Next again for the preview. It shows the exam name, the type and the period. Dates Set reads zero, because the subject dates are optional and can be added later from the Date Sheet. Tap Create.

00:01:30.487 --> 00:01:38.623
A screen confirms that the exam was created. Tap Done, and the new exam appears in the list, ready for marks.

00:01:45.345 --> 00:01:50.625
Your exam is created. Next, you can enter marks for it.
